NOTE 3: The human-readable network name per SNPN is only used for manual SNPN selection. If the SNPN supports Localized Service, the human-readable network name of the SNPN can be information related to the Localized Service. The mechanism how human-readable network name is provided (i.e. whether it is broadcasted or unicasted) to the UE is specified in TS 38.331 [28].
- Information, as described in TS 38.300 [27], TS 38.331 [28] and in TS 38.304 [50], to prevent UEs not supporting SNPNs from accessing the cell, e.g. if the cell only provides access to non-public networks;
